  "problem": "Let $V$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in Q.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. The zero-polynomial belongs to $V.$\n\nII. For the zero-polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in V,$ we have $p(x)+0=p(x).$\n\nIII. For any $p(x),q(x)\\in V,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x).$",
